From: Andrey Korshunov <razor1702@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: set reset button for NanoPi R28S

The board has a single user button. Report it as KEY_RESTART so
gpio-button-hotplug treats it as the reset button, the way every other
OpenWrt router with one button behaves.

Signed-off-by: Andrey Korshunov <razor1702@gmail.com>

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-nanopi-r28s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-nanopi-r28s.dts
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
 			debounce-interval = <50>;
 			gpios = <&gpio4 RK_PB2 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 			label = "USER";
-			linux,code = <BTN_1>;
+			linux,code = <KEY_RESTART>;
 			wakeup-source;
 		};
 	};
